<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Peace of Thorn</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1466">1466</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Peace of Toruń (1466) · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirteen-years-war-1454-1466">Thirteen Years' War (1454–1466)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second Peace of Thorn, signed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/torun">Toruń</a> in October 1466, ended the Thirteen Years' War between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>. Western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>, with Danzig and the Order's former capital Marienburg, became Royal Prussia under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Polish crown</a>, together with the bishopric of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chelmno">Culm</a>. The rest of the Order's state was held as a Polish fief.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-peace-of-thorn.jpg" alt="Second Peace of Thorn" width="320" height="176" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marian Jaroczyński (from 1873) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2nd_peace_of_torun.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
